      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s your current goal / timeline for this CL? I don\u0027t want to block things too much, but I\u0027m worried about the relatively lack of structure between modules. While it is workable for a prototype, we are landing in the real repo and as code grows we\u0027ll really need boundaries between modules.\n\nWhat that look like is:\n\n - dawn::native is not used outside of dawn::native (only the webgpu.h and DawnNative.h + backend headers are the public API) (some white box tests use it directly but they are clearly tests of the internals of dawn::native).\n - Capture / replay should probably two separate libs that use the same de/serialization lib. This is both to ensure their interface with each other is the serialization format, and to avoid a `dawn::native` -(for capture)-\u003e `dawn::replay` -(for replay)-\u003e `dawn::native` cyclic dependency.\n - Replay should have its own public API in `include/dawn/replay` (this is less immediately important because it doesn\u0027t cause issues with the rest of the codebase).",
      "revId": "1649210388f5eae077e9e440a0d14406bdc70c89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
